From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] vkr: Vulkan Video (sessions, parameters and coding commands)

Vulkan Video through Venus: VK_KHR_video_queue, video_decode_queue, video_decode_h264/h265/av1/vp9, video_encode_queue,
video_encode_h264/h265 and video_maintenance1/2, advertised as far as the host's driver has them. Neither virglrenderer nor Mesa's Venus
had any; on NVIDIA hosts it is the way to NVENC from the guest (VA-API on NVIDIA decodes only).

- venus-protocol regenerated from 9fa07f3 (this tree's) plus WinBoat's generator changes: the codec types of
  video.xml (StdVideo*: bitfield flag structs and 2-D arrays as blobs, H.265 HRD sub-layer arrays at their maximum
  length), the extensions above, command types 1000-1015 (clear of upstream's numbering; the guest's Mesa uses
  the same), a "video" command group, and sizeof for the outputs of commands that also reply with a blob
  (vkGetEncodedVideoSessionParametersKHR), and int8_t/int16_t as primitives (the codecs' PPS, slice headers and weight tables), and len names that start with a capital (AV1's tile arrays); a NULL output pointer ahead of a blob decoded in place (vkGetEncodedVideoSessionParametersKHR without
  feedback) keeps its marker's room, or the blob landed 8 bytes early under the size.
- vkr_video.c: the physical-device queries, sessions and session parameters as tracked objects (destroyed with
  the device), memory requirements and binding, encoded session parameters, and the five coding commands.
- vkr_common.c: the extensions in vkr's own list.
- vkr_device_object.py: an object's commands can be in a protocol header of another name ("protocol_header").
